\begin_layout Plain Layout

A tree is generated from the operators $
\backslash
{a,b,2,3
\backslash
}$ and the terminals $
\backslash
cdot,-,/$.
 Only a tree created with the full-method has a branching factor high enough
 to create a complex combinations of variables like .
 A grow tree has a lower branching factor and produces more encapsulated
 expressions like $(a-
\backslash
frac{b}{2})*3$, which can be interpreted easier.
 
\end_layout

