\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
All IB features at a glance.
 The reward is not part of the GP-process.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Industrial Benchmark was introduced by scientists at Siemens to meet
 the high requirements of complex, real world industrial processes.
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "industrialBenchmark"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 It is high-dimensional 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "IB-observations-state"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

, yet the Markov process is only partially observable, so even past values
 must also be considered.
 Since it is also very stochastic, the learning process is made even more
 difficult.
 The Reward depends on a combination of Action 0 and Action 1, as well as
 Action 2, which severely penalises misconduct.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Currently there are no good human written solutions known for the IB, but
 approaching the average value (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

do nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) is considered to be a respectably good comparison solution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Black box: PSONN
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As black box, a particle swarm optimisation algorithm with neural networks
 (PSONN 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft"
literal "true"

\end_inset

) with a calculated IB reward of 
\begin_inset Formula $5353$
\end_inset

 was chosen.
 
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The initial states of the IB in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 were randomized.
 Comparable values could be obtained by a randomized initial state, but
 the results were very volatile.
 The difference of agents in Hein's work was 7% worse on average.
 This value was used for comparison.
 For the PSONN policy, this results in a adjusted penalty value of 
\begin_inset Formula $5728/1.07=5353$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Particle swarm optimisation algorithms, similar to GP, can find solutions
 for many types of problems.
 The solution space is populated by a swarm population, which should find
 the best optima by swarm intelligence.
 This approach is very interesting as a black box, because even bulky solution
 models can be found relatively quickly.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Chapter
Approach / Familiarity Genetic Programming
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following, the implementation of the approach to enhance genetic
 programming with familiarity is presented.
 As a reference for familiarity, a heuristic developed by an expert to solve
 a problem (origin) is used.
 As a measure for the changes some factors are presented that have led to
 the use of the Tree Edit Distance (TED), which calculates the number of
 differences of computational trees.
 The fitness of the candidates is calculated as a possible path via a regression
, whose data is generated by black box approaches.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Outline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The approach is based on the point of view of a developer who has dealt
 with a RL problem in detail and has already written a program to solve
 the problem.
 Although the program is already very mature, there is a parallel RL solution
 that works better than the expert's program.
 This solution is considered a black box and therefore cannot be explained.
 The expert's program is now to be modified with genetic programming so
 that it works just as well as the black box, but still stays close enough
 to the expert's program so that the developer can detect the necessary
 changes.
\end_layout

