\begin_layout Section
Latex tree visualisation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The visualisation of the trees was done with the help of latex, where the
 Forest package which arranges nodes in a space-saving way, especially with
 large trees.
 For very large trees, a tight-tree version is also created, were created
 in which branches with simple mathematical formulas (which do not involve
 fixed nodes) are represented as individual nodes.
 This preserves the structure of the tree without inflating it with simple
 mathematical formulas.
 Nodes are combined if they are not fixed and if their expression is part
 of classical mathematical formulas.
 
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Exceptions are operators too, which change between formulas and propositional
 logic:
\begin_inset Formula $\{\min,\max,\text{if},<,=,\}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

