\begin_layout Chapter
Comparison & Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
During the tests on the benchmarks, the main focus is on how the candidates
 of trust-based GP differ from the results of classic GP.
 Since the space of the candidates is artificially changed in trust-based
 GP, it is to be expected that the performance is subject to the classic
 GP.
 The focus was put on the following points:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Familiarity and interpretability of the candidates
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Effects on the performance of the results:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Regression error
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Real reward
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Security and existence of performance outliers
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
All runs were carried out with both MAE and MSE.
 The runs with MSE had in almost all cases the better results in the real
 benchmarks.
 This also allowed them to be better compared with Hein's results.
\end_layout

