\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Domain Expert solutions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The following heuristics are known solutions to MC:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Maximum momentum by accelerating towards the current direction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Preset policy with a parabolic upper and lower limit
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
GP-friendly by trying to give the GP process interfaces for Innovations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The following improvements were also tested, if possible:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Select a central structure with fixed nodes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Always accelerate (ignoring the no-push action).
 In the examples where Action 1 (no acceleration) could not be chosen, the
 regression error can at best decrease to 0.023 for Sarsa-200 and to 0.066
 for Sarsa-75.
 
