\begin_layout Paragraph
Expert reference
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As no expert policy for the IB is known, a policy that is considered to
 be useful was used as a starting solution - but it is not a classic, human
 solution.
 The heuristics followed the tactic of subtracting a certain value from
 the most current variable of the respective action (
\begin_inset Formula $\text{Velocity}_{0},\text{Gain}_{0},\text{Shift}_{0}$
\end_inset

).
 The real performance of the candidates, especially with more complex candidates
, is comparable to all other runs.
 However, the similarity to the start policies remains, either in the form
 of the variables used or also in the form of the basic structure.
\end_layout

